and you could do whatever you wanted.

01:42:22.215 --> 01:42:23.415
And that's not true.

01:42:24.055 --> 01:42:25.015
When

01:42:25.015 --> 01:42:27.655
you do a special permit to put in

01:42:28.140 --> 01:42:30.220
the sign or anything else,

01:42:30.620 --> 01:42:34.620
you have to continue to comply with all the other regulations.

01:42:35.500 --> 01:42:43.285
The special permit would require us to have a public hearing where we get input from the public, and maybe there are extenuating circumstances

01:42:43.285 --> 01:42:45.205
where in this particular location

01:42:45.365 --> 01:42:47.285
we don't want to allow

01:42:47.445 --> 01:42:48.645
the maximum.

01:42:50.485 --> 01:42:52.405
And an example of that would be

01:42:52.885 --> 01:42:53.925
when we talked about

01:42:55.040 --> 01:42:56.960
Scott Beebe's kennel.

01:42:58.320 --> 01:42:59.040
And we

01:42:59.360 --> 01:43:02.800
were looking at whether or not a Class A kennel should be

01:43:03.200 --> 01:43:04.960
special permit or not.

01:43:06.480 --> 01:43:11.145
And we chose to say yes, it should be special permit

01:43:11.625 --> 01:43:12.505
because

01:43:13.705 --> 01:43:18.665
there might be a lot that has the right size for a kennel,

01:43:19.785 --> 01:43:20.745
but it's in,

01:43:21.705 --> 01:43:22.665
for some reason,

01:43:22.985 --> 01:43:25.705
it's not the optimum place to put a kennel,

01:43:26.190 --> 01:43:29.630
and we could not approve it based on that.

01:43:29.870 --> 01:43:30.830
So it's not,

01:43:31.630 --> 01:43:36.990
the special permit with a public hearing does not allow us to abandon all the regulations.

01:43:37.390 --> 01:43:40.270
It allows us to use extra judicial

01:43:43.395 --> 01:43:50.515
insight. There might be some extenuating reasons why we wouldn't want it where it's going be put. It allows us to act on that.

01:43:52.035 --> 01:43:52.675
So anyhow,

01:43:53.950 --> 01:44:01.710
that's how I think we got there. We said that if we use a special permit, we don't have to comply with the regs. But I don't know that for a fact. That's just a guess.

01:44:05.870 --> 01:44:10.735
All right. Okay, so I'm going to put 32 square foot window space and

01:44:11.375 --> 01:44:16.015
we'll let Jim figure out if there's anything in the record that shows how we got there.

01:44:17.775 --> 01:44:18.655
Next issue,

01:44:19.310 --> 01:44:20.590
political signs.

01:44:20.750 --> 01:44:23.550
And as I may have mentioned, I got an email back from

01:44:23.790 --> 01:44:24.910
Mark Brandt's

01:44:24.910 --> 01:44:26.830
late this afternoon that

01:44:27.230 --> 01:44:31.870
apologized profusely for not getting back sooner, but for

01:44:32.365 --> 01:44:36.445
some reason he'd been completely crazy for the last two weeks.

01:44:38.285 --> 01:44:39.165
But his

01:44:40.365 --> 01:44:41.085
thought

01:44:41.485 --> 01:44:42.765
was that,

01:44:44.925 --> 01:44:46.045
like I was suggesting,

01:44:47.680 --> 01:44:48.880
we consolidated

01:44:48.880 --> 01:44:52.000
a lot of signs into temporary signs.

01:44:53.840 --> 01:44:56.080
And maybe a political sign

01:44:56.320 --> 01:45:00.000
isn't a temporary sign. I was going put some regulation where,

01:45:00.240 --> 01:45:08.755
you know, posted for longer than eighteen months, like it says here, requires a permit. We said that in our current wording for temporary signs.

01:45:10.675 --> 01:45:17.155
Attorney Branch pointed out that there are some people out there who don't think the twenty

01:45:16.250 --> 01:45:18.570
twenty election is over yet.

01:45:19.610 --> 01:45:23.610
And so we are way beyond election day and

01:45:25.370 --> 01:45:26.490
coming into

01:45:26.490 --> 01:45:31.130
where it's certainly not a temporary site anymore if we put some kind of length on that.

01:45:32.295 --> 01:45:33.735
But what we did

01:45:34.215 --> 01:45:39.175
for the last election cycle that both the political parties seemed to be happy with

01:45:39.415 --> 01:45:42.855
is we said you can put signs up no more than 10 foot high,

01:45:43.015 --> 01:45:46.855
no more than 32 square feet, no more than 50 square feet total,

01:45:48.190 --> 01:45:48.830
and

01:45:50.030 --> 01:45:51.070
it could be

01:45:53.950 --> 01:45:54.830
up for

01:45:54.990 --> 01:45:59.150
whenever you want to put it up and take it down whenever is appropriate.

01:45:59.470 --> 01:46:02.590
They mostly all came down within a week or so after the election.

01:46:05.195 --> 01:46:06.635
One of the things that

01:46:07.675 --> 01:46:12.315
that was not stressed in the last go around that is not a change,

01:46:12.715 --> 01:46:15.755
but consistent with our previous regs is

01:46:17.190 --> 01:46:17.830
the

01:46:18.630 --> 01:46:26.950
signs can't be posted on, they can be posted on town property like out at the dump town hall and that sort of thing, but not in the town right away.

01:46:27.590 --> 01:46:31.430
That varies a little bit, but it's generally within 10 feet at the edge of the road.

01:46:33.165 --> 01:46:38.365
And it also says you can't put a sign within 15 feet of the yard property lines.

01:46:38.525 --> 01:46:41.405
You know, it's got to be clear that the signs are in your yard.

01:46:42.045 --> 01:46:44.205
And so I left those that wording

01:46:44.630 --> 01:46:47.110
consistent with what used to be there,

01:46:47.510 --> 01:46:48.310
but I think

01:46:49.190 --> 01:46:51.190
everybody would be happy with that.

01:46:51.510 --> 01:46:55.190
But instead of having it lumped into the temporary sign category,

01:46:55.510 --> 01:47:01.855
I wanted to be very clear. You know, shouldn't be having to guess at what the regs are. Here's the rules for political science.

01:47:02.095 --> 01:47:02.575
And

01:47:03.695 --> 01:47:06.575
we get a public hearing before we implement these and

01:47:07.375 --> 01:47:14.780
I would invite both of the heads of the political parties over here so that they could have their say and we make sure that we hear from them.

01:47:15.100 --> 01:47:16.780
But I think they would be happy with that.

01:47:17.260 --> 01:47:17.980
>> Why

01:47:18.140 --> 01:47:22.140
Jed would we want to have a political sign up for more than,

01:47:22.460 --> 01:47:23.100
you know,

01:47:23.900 --> 01:47:26.860
a couple months maybe at the very outside I would say.

01:47:27.745 --> 01:47:28.705
>> I wouldn't.

01:47:29.505 --> 01:47:30.865
But the courts have said

01:47:31.345 --> 01:47:33.825
that you can't. It's a free speech issue.

01:47:34.385 --> 01:47:39.025
The courts have said we cannot limit the amount of time that a political sign is up.

01:47:39.680 --> 01:47:40.560
And how can We

01:47:41.360 --> 01:47:48.640
can only limit a political sign to the maximum that we allow in our other signs for those areas.

01:47:48.880 --> 01:47:50.880
And so that's why you get

01:47:52.495 --> 01:47:59.535
nowhere in our regs do we say a sign could be more than 32 square feet. So that's why the biggest political sign is 32 square feet.

01:48:00.255 --> 01:48:03.615
And nowhere in our regs do we say that you can have signage

01:48:03.890 --> 01:48:05.970
in excess of 50 square feet.

01:48:06.610 --> 01:48:08.850
Now, I think maybe out in the business zone,

01:48:09.170 --> 01:48:13.170
you might be able to have signage more than that, but that's what we limited it to

01:48:13.490 --> 01:48:19.915
so that I could say that's the limit for the political signs too. Then we just don't get too crazy with those.

01:48:21.355 --> 01:48:23.595
But I would like to have

01:48:23.835 --> 01:48:29.995
the sign, you know, if I were to make the rules, I would say sixty days before the election, seven days after the election,

01:48:30.790 --> 01:48:33.430
that's that's your window, but that's

01:48:33.750 --> 01:48:34.870
been deemed

01:48:35.110 --> 01:48:36.470
unconstitutional.

01:48:38.310 --> 01:48:41.910
Because somewhere in our regulations, have eighteen months?

01:48:42.390 --> 01:48:44.230
>> We do. That's what,

01:48:45.585 --> 01:48:48.545
well, it actually, our current regulations

01:48:48.545 --> 01:48:49.505
specify

01:48:49.665 --> 01:48:51.905
that you can't post a

01:48:52.465 --> 01:48:54.465
political election sign

01:48:55.265 --> 01:48:57.345
more than thirty days prior to the election.

01:48:58.240 --> 01:49:01.920
And at the last go around, we agreed that that was

01:49:02.720 --> 01:49:04.640
too restrictive and

01:49:04.720 --> 01:49:06.640
we agreed to sixty days.

01:49:07.760 --> 01:49:10.800
I don't know if sixty days is good enough now. But

01:49:11.920 --> 01:49:12.480
clearly,

01:49:13.815 --> 01:49:19.255
more than thirty days is necessary because a lot of people had already voted thirty days prior to the election.

01:49:19.975 --> 01:49:23.335
They said, why put it up now? Everybody has got their mind made up.

01:49:24.615 --> 01:49:25.175
That

01:49:25.895 --> 01:49:26.935
is what

01:49:27.440 --> 01:49:30.560
and our old reg said that the zoning

01:49:32.160 --> 01:49:33.120
commission

01:49:33.360 --> 01:49:35.600
could extend that to ninety days.

01:49:36.160 --> 01:49:38.320
But ninety days isn't

01:49:39.135 --> 01:49:44.655
based on anything either. And so that's why I was just going to take out the time limit for it and

01:49:45.695 --> 01:49:46.415
hopefully,

01:49:46.495 --> 01:49:47.535
you know, we

01:49:48.575 --> 01:49:51.215
can be kind of reasonable. I think most

01:49:51.535 --> 01:49:53.135
of the political signs I see,

01:49:53.880 --> 01:49:55.480
you know, are down

01:49:55.880 --> 01:50:01.959
now. There's a couple not to do with any election that are still up, but are kind of political in nature

01:50:02.200 --> 01:50:03.480
and are protected

01:50:03.560 --> 01:50:04.520
by free speech.

01:50:08.705 --> 01:50:09.905
>> Well, are some

01:50:10.225 --> 01:50:12.065
pretty large ones that are

01:50:14.385 --> 01:50:16.305
regarding a specific candidate,

01:50:16.305 --> 01:50:16.705
right?

01:50:18.225 --> 01:50:22.390
And those are longer than eighteen months. So how would we,

01:50:24.230 --> 01:50:30.550
how would you enforce that? You'd tell them they need a permit and then they'd apply for the permit and they'd still keep it up, right?

01:50:31.110 --> 01:50:34.470
>> Well, and that gets into the rope with the temporary signs.

01:50:35.645 --> 01:50:38.045
Has been viewed as unconstitutional.

01:50:38.525 --> 01:50:41.005
I cannot put a time limit on those signs.

01:50:41.565 --> 01:50:45.805
Now I'm not aware of those signs in Andover right now,

01:50:46.125 --> 01:50:52.150
but I've seen them other places. And again, my exposure to signs is pretty much as I walk around the lake.

01:50:52.390 --> 01:50:52.870
But

01:50:55.590 --> 01:50:56.310
>> anyhow,

01:50:58.710 --> 01:50:59.510
I think,

01:50:59.830 --> 01:51:06.605
you know, we are on firm footing, limiting the sign to 32 square feet. And I did see a couple of those

01:51:06.925 --> 01:51:09.005
primarily along Route 6

01:51:09.165 --> 01:51:10.685
during election season.

01:51:13.485 --> 01:51:15.245
But at least it puts

01:51:15.725 --> 01:51:19.325
an upper limit on what can be out there

01:51:21.300 --> 01:51:22.740
that's defensible.

01:51:24.660 --> 01:51:25.300
And

01:51:25.940 --> 01:51:31.060
same thing with the 50 square feet total. If somebody had a, you know, I think

01:51:31.940 --> 01:51:33.380
the average

01:51:33.825 --> 01:51:37.025
little election sign is normally about three square feet.

01:51:37.345 --> 01:51:44.865
That would give somebody to put like 16 signs in their yard before they exceed the 50 square foot limit if they were all that.

01:51:45.825 --> 01:51:50.190
And that's plenty. I think the most I saw last year walking around was 10 or 12,

01:51:50.590 --> 01:51:51.150
but

01:51:52.350 --> 01:51:54.350
that was plenty of signs.

01:51:56.030 --> 01:52:05.294
And so that's what I'm thinking on political signs at this point. I'll just put something in, here are the rules for political signs, they meet all the constitutional requirements for free speech.

01:52:08.095 --> 01:52:09.055
If

01:52:09.055 --> 01:52:09.774
somebody,

01:52:11.375 --> 01:52:14.575
again, there have been a couple of signs that have been very offensive.

01:52:16.010 --> 01:52:16.650
And

01:52:18.810 --> 01:52:21.050
we cannot go tell them to take it down.

01:52:21.370 --> 01:52:24.570
We can have somebody go out and talk to them and ask them to take them down,

01:52:25.530 --> 01:52:27.770
but that's really all we can do in that case.

01:52:31.775 --> 01:52:36.335
But I wanted to break it out. I think we collected a bunch of signs into temporary signs,

01:52:36.415 --> 01:52:40.415
pendulum swung a little too far, wanted to back it off just a little bit.

01:52:40.895 --> 01:52:43.615
You put a special paragraph on political signs in there.

01:52:46.080 --> 01:52:49.360
>> I think it's great, Jed. I just question how

01:52:49.600 --> 01:52:51.440
enforceable this is gonna be

01:52:52.160 --> 01:52:56.080
if people don't wanna take their signs down. Well, we can't enforce it. Yeah,

01:52:57.905 --> 01:52:59.425
>> It is unenforceable.

01:52:59.425 --> 01:53:06.385
That's why I'm going take this thing that says posted longer than eighteen months requires a permit. I'm going to get rid of that part there.

01:53:07.105 --> 01:53:08.305
You know, we just can't do it.

01:53:13.110 --> 01:53:14.790
Okay, then the third

01:53:14.790 --> 01:53:19.749
thing that I wanted to split out, you know, I didn't like the way in

01:53:19.910 --> 01:53:28.175
temporary signs, and again, now I come down to temporary signs are like tag sale signs, the steak fry dinner at the firehouse sign,

01:53:28.655 --> 01:53:32.735
selling plants at Easter or over at the firehouse or something,

01:53:33.135 --> 01:53:34.975
those kinds of things. Temporary

01:53:35.695 --> 01:53:36.095
signs,

01:53:38.000 --> 01:53:40.000
I forget whether it was sixty days

01:53:40.560 --> 01:53:43.200
or whatever taken down seven days after.

01:53:44.560 --> 01:53:46.880
I think that's good for the temporary signs.

01:53:47.840 --> 01:53:55.365
I was confused. I didn't like the wording, is it specified to real estate signs? Because some of those signs are up a lot.

01:53:55.685 --> 01:54:02.405
You you don't know when you're going to sell your place. Right now it sells in two days, but that's not always been the case. And

01:54:03.470 --> 01:54:06.270
it might be longer than a temporary sign there.

01:54:06.590 --> 01:54:10.510
I think most of the signs come down within a week of the sale actually going

01:54:10.590 --> 01:54:11.870
through. And so

01:54:12.510 --> 01:54:17.550
that's that. And I was going put if longer than eighteen months requires a permit.

01:54:18.905 --> 01:54:22.745
Because when I talked about getting rid of how long the real

01:54:23.065 --> 01:54:31.225
estate sign could be up, attorney branch was talking about there are properties over in Glastonbury that are for lease

01:54:31.920 --> 01:54:38.560
and there's always something for lease. And so they've had the for lease sign up for years over there and

01:54:38.720 --> 01:54:47.440
he wanted to have some kind of a bounds on that. And so that's where I was putting the posted for longer than eighteen months requires a permit. And so

01:54:47.815 --> 01:54:48.695
I

01:54:49.335 --> 01:54:57.095
don't know that that will do any good. I don't know that we can enforce it, but if somebody makes a complaint that gives us something to cite,

01:54:57.095 --> 01:55:03.970
and then the guy's got to come in and get a permit, there's a given burden with that, that it might be just easier to take the sign down.

01:55:04.450 --> 01:55:10.050
And then you're going to see, that's where you're going to get into. He takes the sign down for a week, puts it back up, resets the clock.

01:55:10.690 --> 01:55:13.330
And so we probably can't win that either, but

01:55:14.225 --> 01:55:20.465
we can give our best to show what the expectation is. I haven't seen the real estate signs be abused,

01:55:21.265 --> 01:55:22.545
so yeah,

01:55:22.945 --> 01:55:24.305
I think not

01:55:24.385 --> 01:55:24.785
a problem.

01:55:26.960 --> 01:55:30.720
And that's all that I wanted to talk about on signs.

01:55:30.880 --> 01:55:34.320
I'll go into build those in there. I think we're getting pretty close.

01:55:37.855 --> 01:55:40.575
And I'll show you an updated version

01:55:40.975 --> 01:55:50.255
hopefully a month from now and we can decide if we're good to go or, you know, and schedule a public hearing with it with all this other stuff that we wanted to do.

01:55:51.830 --> 01:55:54.149
>> So, can we just go over something?

01:55:55.030 --> 01:55:55.590
Just

01:55:55.990 --> 01:55:57.990
so I understand this correctly.

01:55:58.310 --> 01:56:02.790
Yep. The gas stations, those signs are well over 32 square feet.

01:56:03.645 --> 01:56:08.685
The big, the big signs. Yep. So, even if they did come before

01:56:09.965 --> 01:56:12.205
the appeals board and got a

01:56:13.085 --> 01:56:15.805
an action that said that they could build their

01:56:16.045 --> 01:56:16.765
whatever it is,

01:56:17.510 --> 01:56:26.070
size square foot they're over then their sign limit is up is that what you're saying that there's no more signs to be put up on that premise?

01:56:26.230 --> 01:56:28.310
>> So one of the one of the things that

01:56:29.125 --> 01:56:32.245
we did change in all the spots

01:56:32.965 --> 01:56:35.205
in here is that if

01:56:38.725 --> 01:56:40.325
a special permit,

01:56:40.885 --> 01:56:43.365
like let's talk about the piece of property

01:56:44.330 --> 01:56:46.649
by the Ben Franklin Place.

01:56:47.370 --> 01:56:49.290
They're

01:56:49.290 --> 01:56:50.010
going to come

01:56:50.570 --> 01:56:53.609
through planning and zoning with the site plan to build

01:56:54.330 --> 01:56:55.130
a store.

01:56:56.905 --> 01:57:01.065
And one of the things that we can ask for on that site plan,

01:57:01.465 --> 01:57:04.585
we should ask for, is the proposed signage.

01:57:06.745 --> 01:57:07.945
And so

01:57:08.760 --> 01:57:14.600
that is where we can make sure that the signage that's proposed is

01:57:15.400 --> 01:57:17.640
consistent with our regulations.

01:57:19.720 --> 01:57:21.880
I think there may have been times,

01:57:22.280 --> 01:57:23.400
and the one that

01:57:23.815 --> 01:57:29.975
I am aware of that I'll go back to was right after I got on the Planning and Zoning Commission

01:57:30.215 --> 01:57:33.415
where we had the home occupation

01:57:33.975 --> 01:57:36.935
for the fella off

01:57:38.270 --> 01:57:39.390
River Road

01:57:40.750 --> 01:57:44.190
behind the ball fields over there for his home property.

01:57:45.870 --> 01:57:50.750
And the way it was explained to me as I started asking questions about the regulations

01:57:50.750 --> 01:57:51.470
is

01:57:51.725 --> 01:57:55.245
this is a special permit, the regulations don't apply.

01:57:57.245 --> 01:58:01.965
And I was new at the time and I said, okay, I didn't like it.

01:58:04.205 --> 01:58:05.085
But

01:58:06.210 --> 01:58:11.810
that's what I heard. I won't say that's what was said, I will always say that's

01:58:11.810 --> 01:58:12.690
what I heard

01:58:13.010 --> 01:58:15.730
and nobody wanted to talk about the regulations.

01:58:18.705 --> 01:58:23.745
After I got to be chairman, I studied the regulations a little more and it says

01:58:24.385 --> 01:58:29.025
that with a special permit, you do have to follow all the regulations,

01:58:29.505 --> 01:58:31.025
but you have to have a public hearing.

01:58:32.600 --> 01:58:33.480
And so

01:58:34.920 --> 01:58:43.640
that's why I think that those gas stations might be that way. I asked Jim again to pull the file just so we can see if there's any clues in there

01:58:43.960 --> 01:58:49.135
as to how we got to where we did. But if the Planning and Zoning Commission authorized that,

01:58:49.535 --> 01:58:52.655
I think they're good to go. I don't think there's anything we can do about it.

01:58:53.055 --> 01:58:55.855
It's just like if the zoning agent makes a

01:58:56.815 --> 01:58:58.815
ruling on those things that he has,

01:58:59.960 --> 01:59:02.040
you know, cognizance over,

01:59:03.640 --> 01:59:04.760
that's his business.

01:59:06.360 --> 01:59:10.120
But first is to find out what's in the files to

01:59:10.680 --> 01:59:14.040
have a clue as to how did we get to where we are today because

01:59:14.405 --> 01:59:17.365
I can't see how we got there looking at our wrecks.

01:59:23.445 --> 01:59:29.550
>> I think it probably is just improvements over the years. And that could be too. Nobody

01:59:29.870 --> 01:59:30.910
questioned it.

01:59:31.310 --> 01:59:33.630
>> And one of the things that we have learned,

01:59:33.870 --> 01:59:36.270
and Jim pointed out was a

01:59:37.710 --> 01:59:40.990
concern of his, is that if we approve

01:59:41.675 --> 01:59:42.715
signage,

01:59:44.395 --> 01:59:46.315
is the Planning and Zoning Commission,

01:59:47.035 --> 01:59:49.435
if somebody wants to change the signage,

01:59:49.515 --> 01:59:51.995
they have to come back before the Planning and Zoning Commission.

